## 📌 Overview

This project deploys **SmolVLM2** — a multimodal vision-language model — on the **AMD Kria KV260 FPGA SOM** using a hybrid CPU+FPGA co-design approach. The vision encoder runs on the FPGA's **DPU (Deep learning Processing Unit)**, while the transformer decoder runs on the **ARM Cortex-A53 CPU cores**, achieving significant throughput improvements over a CPU-only baseline.

### Key Achievements

| Metric | CPU-Only Baseline | FPGA Accelerated | Improvement |
|--------|:-----------------:|:----------------:|:-----------:|
| Prefill Throughput | ~65 tok/s | ~312 tok/s | **+378%** |
| Decode Throughput | ~14 tok/s | ~58 tok/s | **+314%** |
| OCRBench Accuracy | — | **62%** (100 samples) | — |
| Vision Encoder Latency | ~1840 ms (CPU) | ~248 ms (DPU) | **7.4×** |

### Two Deployment Approaches

| | Approach 1 — 256M ⭐ | Approach 2 — 500M |
|---|---|---|
| **Model** | SmolVLM2-256M-Instruct | SmolVLM2-500M-Video-Instruct |
| **Vision Encoder** | FPGA DPU INT8 | FPGA DPU INT8 + Pruned |
| **LM Decoder** | ARM CPU FP32/INT8 | ARM CPU QAT INT8 |
| **Pruning** | ✗ Not needed | ✓ L1 channel (25%) + Taylor head (20%) |
| **QAT Fine-tuning** | ✗ Not needed | ✓ TextVQA (5000 samples) |
| **RAM Usage** | ~750 MB INT8 | ~776 MB INT8 |
| **Recommended for** | ✅ Preliminary round | ✅ Final round |

---

## 🏗️ Architecture

```
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│                    KV260 Inference Pipeline                      │
│                                                                  │
│  Image + Question                                                │
│       │                                                          │
│       ▼                                                          │
│  ┌─────────────────┐  ARM CPU                                    │
│  │ Preprocessing   │  Resize → Normalize → NCHW tensor           │
│  └────────┬────────┘                                             │
│           │  (1, 3, 224, 224)                                    │
│           ▼                                                      │
│  ┌─────────────────┐  FPGA DPU  ← INT8 compiled .xmodel         │
│  │ Vision Encoder  │  SigLIP ViT — dense conv ops                │
│  │   (SigLIP)      │  DSP parallelization + BRAM buffering        │
│  └────────┬────────┘                                             │
│           │  (1, 256, 768) visual embeddings                     │
│           ▼                                                      │
│  ┌─────────────────┐  ARM CPU                                    │
│  │ Projection MLP  │  Feature bridging layer                     │
│  └────────┬────────┘                                             │
│           │                                                      │
│           ▼                                                      │
│  ┌─────────────────┐  ARM CPU  ← KV Cache enabled                │
│  │ Transformer     │  Prefill: full context attention             │
│  │ Decoder (LM)    │  Decode: autoregressive + KV cache reuse    │
│  └────────┬────────┘                                             │
│           │                                                      │
│           ▼                                                      │
│      Generated Answer                                            │
└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

### Component Deployment Map

| Component | Platform | Reason |
|-----------|----------|--------|
| Image Preprocessing | ARM CPU | Low compute, simple ops |
| Vision Encoder (SigLIP) | **FPGA DPU** | Dense conv/matmul — maps to DSPs perfectly |
| Projection Layer (MLP) | ARM CPU | Bridging layer, small footprint |
| Transformer Decoder | ARM CPU | Sequential autoregressive — cache-friendly on CPU |
| KV Cache | On-chip DDR4 | Avoids recomputing attention at each decode step |

---

## 📦 Datasets

This project uses **3 unique dataset sources** across **4 distinct uses**:

| # | Dataset | Source | Samples | Purpose | Approach |
|---|---------|--------|:-------:|---------|:--------:|
| 1 | **OCRBench** | `echo840/OCRBench` | 250 | INT8 PTQ Calibration | Both |
| 2 | **OCRBench** | `echo840/OCRBench` | 100 | Accuracy Evaluation | Both |
| 3 | **TextVQA** | `textvqa/textvqa` | 5,000 | QAT Fine-tuning | 500M only |
| 4 | **Synthetic OCR** | Auto-generated | 500 | Pruning Calibration | 500M only |

### Download All Datasets — Single Command

```bash
# 256M approach (OCRBench only — calibration + evaluation)
python download_datasets.py --approach 256M

# 500M approach (all 3 sources)
python download_datasets.py --approach 500M

# Verify what's on disk
python download_datasets.py --verify
```

---

## ⚡ Quick Start

### Prerequisites

- **OS**: Ubuntu 20.04 / 22.04
- **Python**: 3.9
- **Docker**: 20.x or later (for Vitis-AI container)
- **VS Code** with extensions: `Remote-SSH`, `Python`, `Docker`, `Jupyter`
- **KV260 Board**: SSH access configured

### Clone & Setup

```bash
git clone https://github.com/<your-username>/kv260-vlm-accelerator.git
cd kv260-vlm-accelerator

# Create virtual environment
python3.9 -m venv .venv && source .venv/bin/activate

# Install dependencies
pip install --upgrade pip
pip install torch==2.1.0 torchvision==0.16.0 --index-url https://download.pytorch.org/whl/cpu
pip install transformers==4.40.0 accelerate onnx onnxruntime onnxoptimizer
pip install pillow numpy datasets huggingface_hub tqdm scipy matplotlib opencv-python
```

### Run End-to-End (256M Approach)

```bash
# Stage 1 — Download model + datasets
python 01_model_preparation/download_model.py
python download_datasets.py --approach 256M

# Stage 2 — Export to ONNX
python 02_onnx_export/export_vision_encoder.py
python 02_onnx_export/validate_onnx.py

# Stage 3 — Quantize + Compile (inside Vitis-AI Docker)
bash docker_launch.sh
# Inside container:
conda activate vitis-ai-pytorch
python /workspace/03_quantization/quantize_model.py
bash /workspace/04_compilation/compile_model.sh

# Stage 4 — Deploy to KV260 + Evaluate
bash transfer_to_kv260.sh <BOARD_IP>
# Connect via VS Code Remote-SSH then:
python3 05_deployment/deploy_runtime.py
python3 06_evaluation/ocrbench_eval.py
python3 06_evaluation/performance_benchmark.py --baseline-prefill 65.3 --baseline-decode 14.1
```

