## 🗂️ Project Structure

```
kv260-vlm-accelerator/
│
├── 00_dataset_prep/
│   └── (deprecated — use download_datasets.py instead)
│
├── 01_model_preparation/
│   ├── download_model.py          # Download SmolVLM2 from HuggingFace
│   └── partition_model.py         # Split into vision / projection / LM
│
├── 02_onnx_export/
│   ├── export_vision_encoder.py   # PyTorch → ONNX opset 13
│   └── validate_onnx.py           # Graph check + parity test + latency
│
├── 03_quantization/
│   ├── calibration_reader.py      # CalibrationDataReader class
│   └── quantize_model.py          # INT8 PTQ — vai_q_onnx / onnxruntime
│
├── 04_compilation/
│   ├── compile_model.sh           # ONNX → XIR → .xmodel (vai_c_xir)
│   └── KV260_arch.json            # KV260 DPUCZDX8G architecture descriptor
│
├── 05_deployment/
│   ├── deploy_runtime.py          # KV260 environment + DPU runner check
│   └── inference_pipeline.py      # Full CPU+FPGA hybrid pipeline class
│
├── 06_evaluation/
│   ├── cpu_baseline_benchmark.py  # CPU-only baseline (run FIRST)
│   ├── ocrbench_eval.py           # OCRBench accuracy (100 samples)
│   └── performance_benchmark.py   # Prefill + decode throughput + improvement %
│
├── 07_live_test/
│   └── live_monitor_test.py       # Real-time OpenCV display on monitor
│
├── approach_256M/
│   ├── prepare_256M.py            # All-in-one: export + quantize + compile
│   └── pipeline_256M.py           # 256M hybrid pipeline class
│
├── approach_500M/
│   ├── prune_500M.py              # L1 channel pruning + Taylor head pruning
│   ├── quantize_aware_train_500M.py  # QAT fine-tuning on TextVQA
│   └── pipeline_500M.py           # 500M split pipeline with bitsandbytes
│
├── datasets/
│   └── dataset_registry.py        # Dataset documentation + config constants
│
├── download_datasets.py           # ⭐ Single file — downloads ALL datasets
├── run_approach.py                # Master entry point for either approach
├── docker_launch.sh               # Launch Vitis-AI Docker container
├── transfer_to_kv260.sh           # SCP all files to KV260 board
└── requirements.txt
```

