## 📋 Deployment Stages

### Stage 1 — Host Setup, Model Download & Datasets
> **Environment**: VS Code on host machine · Python 3.9 `.venv`

```bash
# Create and activate environment
python3.9 -m venv .venv && source .venv/bin/activate
pip install -r requirements.txt

# Download SmolVLM2-256M (~1 GB)
python 01_model_preparation/download_model.py

# Partition into deployable modules
python 01_model_preparation/partition_model.py

# Download all datasets in one command
python download_datasets.py --approach 256M
```

**✅ Checkpoint**: `models/smolvlm2-256m/` exists · `calibration_dataset/` has 250 images · `eval_dataset/` has 100 images

---

### Stage 2 — ONNX Export & Validation
> **Environment**: VS Code on host · Python 3.9 `.venv`

```bash
# Export vision encoder to ONNX with operator fusion
python 02_onnx_export/export_vision_encoder.py

# Validate: graph integrity + numerical parity + latency benchmark
python 02_onnx_export/validate_onnx.py
```

**✅ Checkpoint**: `models/vision_encoder.onnx` (~370 MB) · `models/vision_encoder_opt.onnx` (~340 MB) · parity diff < 0.001

---

### Stage 3 — INT8 Quantization + DPU Compilation
> **Environment**: Vitis-AI Docker container · attached via VS Code Docker extension

```bash
# Launch container (mounts project as /workspace)
bash docker_launch.sh

# Attach VS Code: Docker sidebar → right-click vitis-ai-kv260 → Attach Visual Studio Code
# Then in container terminal:
conda activate vitis-ai-pytorch

# INT8 Post-Training Quantization (uses OCRBench calibration images)
python /workspace/03_quantization/quantize_model.py

# Compile for KV260 DPU
bash /workspace/04_compilation/compile_model.sh
```

> ⚠️ **Must run inside the Vitis-AI container.** `vai_q_onnx` and `vai_c_xir` are only available in the container. Running outside falls back to CPU-only onnxruntime quantization which cannot be compiled for DPU.

**✅ Checkpoint**: `models/vision_encoder_int8.onnx` (~93 MB) · `compiled_model/vision_encoder.xmodel` (~24 MB) · at least one `[DPU]` subgraph in compilation log

---

### Stage 4 — KV260 Deploy, Live Test & Evaluation
> **Environment**: VS Code Remote-SSH → KV260 board · VART runtime

```bash
# Transfer files to board
bash transfer_to_kv260.sh <BOARD_IP>

# Connect VS Code: Ctrl+Shift+P → Remote-SSH: Connect to Host → kv260-board

# On board — verify all systems
python3 05_deployment/deploy_runtime.py

# Live monitor test (OpenCV window with real-time inference)
export DISPLAY=:0
python3 07_live_test/live_monitor_test.py \
    --source eval_dataset \
    --xmodel compiled_model/vision_encoder.xmodel \
    --model-dir models/smolvlm2-256m

# Measure CPU-only baseline first
python3 06_evaluation/cpu_baseline_benchmark.py

# OCRBench accuracy (100 samples — competition metric)
python3 06_evaluation/ocrbench_eval.py

# Throughput benchmark (replace values with actual baseline from above)
python3 06_evaluation/performance_benchmark.py \
    --baseline-prefill 65.3 \
    --baseline-decode 14.1
```

**✅ Checkpoint**: OpenCV window displayed · `ocrbench_results.json` saved · `benchmark_results.json` saved with positive improvement rates

