## 🖥️ Live Monitor Test

The live monitor test renders real-time VLM inference results in an OpenCV window on any connected display.

```
┌────────────────────────────────────────────────┐  FPS: 1.2
│                                                │
│          [ Live image / webcam frame ]         │
│                                                │
│                                                │
│                                                │
├────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ Q: What text appears in this image?            │
│ A: The sign reads "STOP"                       │
│ Prefill: 248ms  |  Decode: 534ms               │
└────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

### Display Options

| Method | Command |
|--------|---------|
| HDMI (KV260 → monitor) | `export DISPLAY=:0` |
| X11 forwarding (SSH) | `ssh -X ubuntu@<BOARD_IP>` then `export DISPLAY=localhost:10.0` |
| VNC server | `vncserver :1` then connect via VNC viewer |
| Headless (save frames) | Add `--headless` flag — saves to `outputs/` |

### Keyboard Controls

| Key | Action |
|-----|--------|
| `Q` | Quit |
| `P` | Pause / Resume |
| `N` | Next image (folder mode) |
| `S` | Save current frame + answer |
| `1–4` | Switch question type |

---

## 🔧 Hardware Optimizations

### FPGA (DPU Fabric)
- **DSP Parallelization** — vision encoder conv layers mapped to 512 DSPs simultaneously
- **BRAM Buffering** — activation maps cached on-chip to minimize DDR bandwidth
- **Pipeline Design** — DPU instruction pipeline keeps all DSPs busy
- **INT8 QDQ Format** — Vitis-AI QDQ quantization produces DPU-native instructions

### Software (ARM CPU)
- **KV Cache Reuse** — key-value pairs cached across decode steps (`use_cache=True`)
- **Async FPGA+CPU Scheduling** — threaded pipeline overlaps FPGA vision encoding with CPU tokenization
- **Operator Fusion** — Conv+BN, MatMul+BiasAdd fused before compilation via onnxoptimizer
- **Low CPU Memory Mode** — `low_cpu_mem_usage=True` keeps KV260 RAM under 3.5 GB

### 500M Approach Additional
- **L1 Channel Pruning** — removes 25% of least-important conv channels before quantization
- **Taylor Head Pruning** — removes 20% of attention heads by activation importance
- **QAT Fine-tuning** — fake-quantize nodes inserted during TextVQA training to recover accuracy
- **bitsandbytes INT8 Loading** — saves ~500 MB RAM for LM decoder on KV260

---

## 📊 Results

### OCRBench Accuracy (256M, 100 samples)

```
Correct predictions : 62 / 100
Accuracy            : 62.00%
Correctness rule    : ground_truth ⊆ prediction (substring match)
Avg inference time  : 8.4 s / sample
```

### Throughput Benchmark

```
                    CPU-Only    FPGA-Accel    Improvement
─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
Prefill throughput   65.3 tok/s  312.4 tok/s   +378%  (4.78×)
Decode throughput    14.1 tok/s   58.7 tok/s   +316%  (4.16×)
Vision encoder        1842 ms      248 ms        7.4×  faster
Total latency         ~18.5 s     ~8.4 s         2.2×  faster
```

